import{_ as a,o as i,c as t,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.DyLyN3RJ.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"2026-11-11 · Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"2026-11-11 · Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence","outline":false},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-11.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-11.md","lastUpdated":1794364546000}'),n={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-11.md"};function o(s,e,l,c,d,p){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="_2026-11-11-·-agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence" tabindex="-1">2026-11-11 · Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-11-·-agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-11 · Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Key conclusion: enterprise agent governance is becoming concrete in call identity, approval ownership, receipts and failure semantics, while passing tests can still diverge from real deployment. Paperclip staging failures provide a counterexample and Orca cross-host orchestration remains partly inert. The 26 observations support six analyses; analyses are not additional events.</p><h2 id="factual-observations" tabindex="-1">Factual observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#factual-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Factual observations&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="o1-·-codex-execution-identity-during-abort-and-restore" tabindex="-1">O1 · Codex: execution identity during abort and restore <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-·-codex-execution-identity-during-abort-and-restore" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 · Codex: execution identity during abort and restore&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Aborts finalize the correct turn; late unknown aborts preserve another explicitly identified turn. Restored unfinished tool calls receive synthetic aborted outputs, while checks remain for new calls. Aborted does not establish that external side effects never happened.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60700" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-11T02:14:15Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60519" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T04:11:58Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o2-·-codex-delivery-evidence-independent-of-inference" tabindex="-1">O2 · Codex: delivery evidence independent of inference <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-·-codex-delivery-evidence-independent-of-inference" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 · Codex: delivery evidence independent of inference&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Accepted agent messages retain delivery and interaction edges even without another model request. Replay reuses stable item IDs and avoids duplicate receipt items. This improves traceability, without establishing end-to-end exactly-once messaging.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60673" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T22:23:08Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o3-·-codex-call-time-authority-and-identity-revisions" tabindex="-1">O3 · Codex: call-time authority and identity revisions <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-·-codex-call-time-authority-and-identity-revisions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 · Codex: call-time authority and identity revisions&quot;">​</a></h3><p>After asynchronous budget checks, HTTP restarts setup on account changes and WebSocket revalidates the auth owner. Workload identity reuse binds session and provider/mapping/authorization revisions, retaining ordinary refresh continuity but retiring changed identities.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60436" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T19:50:49Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60433" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T19:27:25Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o4-·-codex-managed-policy-templates-and-terminal-denials" tabindex="-1">O4 · Codex: managed policy templates and terminal denials <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-·-codex-managed-policy-templates-and-terminal-denials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 · Codex: managed policy templates and terminal denials&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Managed rules use a trusted Guardian template, with migration warnings for two removed auto_review settings. Explicit inference-hook and workspace denials stop retries and compaction fallback. Explicit host templates remain a distinct allowed path.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60646" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T19:30:51Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60511" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T03:21:57Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60480" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T00:54:59Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o5-·-codex-context-trust-versus-tool-annotations" tabindex="-1">O5 · Codex: context trust versus tool annotations <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-·-codex-context-trust-versus-tool-annotations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 · Codex: context trust versus tool annotations&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Goal objectives enter as untrusted context rather than privileged continuation instructions. In automatic approval readOnlyHint wins over conflicting destructive/openWorld hints; explicit prompt and strict review still apply. Annotation precedence is not proof of tool safety.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60342" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T03:58:32Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/60638" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/codex · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T18:33:47Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o6-·-agents-python-nested-approval-ownership-and-guardrail-restoration" tabindex="-1">O6 · Agents Python: nested approval ownership and guardrail restoration <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-·-agents-python-nested-approval-ownership-and-guardrail-restoration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 · Agents Python: nested approval ownership and guardrail restoration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RunState records nested approval ownership and validates child versus parent-response membership. Calls from different agents remain distinct despite identical IDs/arguments. Missing owners produce an explicit error; insufficient evidence fails closed. Guardrail results survive approval, final results and checkpoints.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/5629" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-python · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T05:47:10Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/5630" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-python · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T05:47:11Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/5633" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-python · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T05:48:25Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/5643" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-python · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T06:56:10Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o7-·-agents-python-recheck-guardrails-before-streams" tabindex="-1">O7 · Agents Python: recheck guardrails before streams <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-·-agents-python-recheck-guardrails-before-streams" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 · Agents Python: recheck guardrails before streams&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Before every streamed model attempt, including retries, the runner checks recorded input-guardrail rejection. Pending guardrails still allow parallel work; this is not blanket sequential pre-authorization.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/5644" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-python · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T06:56:11Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o8-·-agents-js-pending-approvals-handoff-recovery-and-archive-restore" tabindex="-1">O8 · Agents JS: pending approvals, handoff recovery and archive restore <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-·-agents-js-pending-approvals-handoff-recovery-and-archive-restore" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 · Agents JS: pending approvals, handoff recovery and archive restore&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Automatic compaction waits for approval/result pairing and a successful exchange. Optional handoff errorFunction feeds recoverable errors back to the source agent; fail-fast remains default and existing side effects remain. UnixLocal/Docker validate archives before replacing files.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2288" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-js · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T11:03:56Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2290" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-js · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T23:28:07Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2279" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">openai/openai-agents-js · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T23:30:49Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o9-·-gemini-cli-cancellation-trust-and-original-failures" tabindex="-1">O9 · Gemini CLI: cancellation, trust and original failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-·-gemini-cli-cancellation-trust-and-original-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 · Gemini CLI: cancellation, trust and original failures&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Headless signals clean child process groups/PTYS, persist scheduled calls, synthesize interrupted responses on resume and retain signal exit codes. macOS resolves folder trust before entering the sandbox. MessageBus returns publish failures immediately, although this repository currently has no request() callers.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/30204" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">google-gemini/gemini-cli · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T20:16:27Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/30164" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">google-gemini/gemini-cli · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T20:05:57Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/30189" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">google-gemini/gemini-cli · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T21:19:47Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o10-·-claude-code-released-oauth-and-file-permission-fixes" tabindex="-1">O10 · Claude Code: released OAuth and file-permission fixes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-·-claude-code-released-oauth-and-file-permission-fixes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 · Claude Code: released OAuth and file-permission fixes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Release notes report fixes preventing OAuth secrets crossing hosts on redirects, unprompted read-only Bash outside the sandbox, wrong-directory write checks and missing destination-file deny/protection checks for cp/mv. Changed remote-control settings block new sessions until restart. No local reproduction or fleet-upgrade verification.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.321" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">anthropics/claude-code · RELEASED · 2026-11-09T19:22:30Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o11-·-mansura-habiba-skill-integrity-and-intra-skill-conflicts" tabindex="-1">O11 · Mansura Habiba: skill integrity and intra-skill conflicts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-·-mansura-habiba-skill-integrity-and-intra-skill-conflicts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 · Mansura Habiba: skill integrity and intra-skill conflicts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Lock digests cover all shipped files, executable bits and paths; failed temporary-install verification preserves old cache. Intra-skill conflict tags combine deterministic checks and optional LLM classification, remaining advisory. This related author project is not the official AGENTSAFE artifact.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/mansura-habiba/bulbasaur-skill-cli/pull/20" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mansura-habiba/bulbasaur-skill-cli · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T21:02:49Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/mansura-habiba/bulbasaur-skill-cli/pull/19" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mansura-habiba/bulbasaur-skill-cli · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T21:10:42Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o12-·-ag2-1-3-1-released-sandboxes-and-interoperability" tabindex="-1">O12 · AG2 1.3.1: released sandboxes and interoperability <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-·-ag2-1-3-1-released-sandboxes-and-interoperability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 · AG2 1.3.1: released sandboxes and interoperability&quot;">​</a></h3><p>E2B and boxd backends join shared tool environments. E2B extension never shortens running-command lifetime and does not silently recreate expired sandboxes. Upstream ext-apps documents avoid duplicate ui/initialize. Stable A2UI 1.0 entails message/catalog migration and is distinct from MCP Apps.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/releases/tag/v.1.3.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ag2ai/ag2 · RELEASED · 2026-11-10T21:03:11Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o13-·-mcp-apps-2-1-bidirectional-webmcp-bridge" tabindex="-1">O13 · MCP Apps 2.1: bidirectional WebMCP bridge <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-·-mcp-apps-2-1-bidirectional-webmcp-bridge" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 · MCP Apps 2.1: bidirectional WebMCP bridge&quot;">​</a></h3><p>App.registerTool and document.modelContext bridge both directions, relaying tool changes over Apps channels. Enabled per App by default, it is opt-out and adds no wire messages or host APIs. The expanded discovery surface needs separate authority review and does not replace FCoP task semantics.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps/releases/tag/v2.1.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps · RELEASED · 2026-11-10T22:53:57Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o14-·-paperclip-transactional-receipts-for-document-recovery" tabindex="-1">O14 · Paperclip: transactional receipts for document recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-·-paperclip-transactional-receipts-for-document-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 · Paperclip: transactional receipts for document recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>write_document stores revision and idempotency receipt transactionally with baseRevisionId CAS. Orphan recovery replays a saved result or executes once when receipt evidence establishes non-application. This scoped proof does not imply arbitrary-tool exactly-once.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/20674" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">paperclipai/paperclip · MERGED → master · 2026-11-11T01:05:16Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o15-·-paperclip-delegated-token-work-without-secret-visibility" tabindex="-1">O15 · Paperclip: delegated token work without secret visibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-·-paperclip-delegated-token-work-without-secret-visibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 · Paperclip: delegated token work without secret visibility&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A person-only stopgap was superseded by delegated creation with pendingReveal metadata only. The responsible person&#39;s single reveal activates the credential; concurrent/second reveals conflict. Judge the later merged design, not the superseded restriction; old tokens are not automatically removed.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/20581" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">paperclipai/paperclip · MERGED → master · 2026-11-10T17:31:44Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/20613" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">paperclipai/paperclip · MERGED → master · 2026-11-10T21:13:35Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o16-·-paperclip-state-based-evaluation-and-redeploy-gaps" tabindex="-1">O16 · Paperclip: state-based evaluation and redeploy gaps <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-·-paperclip-state-based-evaluation-and-redeploy-gaps" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 · Paperclip: state-based evaluation and redeploy gaps&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Sixteen chat cases move from brittle wording to persisted state, audit and page structure while retaining false-claim checks. A separate upstream staging census reports 276 failed runs and 63 blocked tasks over 48 hours; prior chaos tests missed replaced container/process spaces. K15 adds redeploy faults. These upstream findings do not prove every incident fixed.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/20600" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">paperclipai/paperclip · MERGED → master · 2026-11-10T19:37:16Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/20679" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">paperclipai/paperclip · MERGED → master · 2026-11-11T02:05:18Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o17-·-orca-cross-host-admission-skeleton-and-chat-cli" tabindex="-1">O17 · Orca: cross-host admission skeleton and chat CLI <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-·-orca-cross-host-admission-skeleton-and-chat-cli" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 · Orca: cross-host admission skeleton and chat CLI&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A paired Orca becomes a real caller on the receiving host, admitted synchronously and scoped to its Run. The sending coordinator/envelope path is not active: this skeleton is inert. Separately merged chat list/read/send/wait enables bridges and agents to continue existing chats. These have different maturity.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/40717" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">stablyai/orca · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T19:56:02Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/40836" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">stablyai/orca · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T22:37:32Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o18-·-orca-credential-visibility-and-opt-in-allowlist" tabindex="-1">O18 · Orca: credential visibility and opt-in allowlist <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-·-orca-credential-visibility-and-opt-in-allowlist" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 · Orca: credential visibility and opt-in allowlist&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Recipe scripts still inherit the process environment by default. Credential variable names are visible and passEnv provides an opt-in allowlist. Malformed configuration falls back to safe base variables rather than full inheritance. Visibility is not default least privilege.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/40757" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">stablyai/orca · MERGED → main · 2026-11-11T01:58:07Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o19-·-orca-awake-time-scheduling-and-failure-classification" tabindex="-1">O19 · Orca: awake-time scheduling and failure classification <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-·-orca-awake-time-scheduling-and-failure-classification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 · Orca: awake-time scheduling and failure classification&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Startup deadlines count awake time, short DarkWake defers catch-up, and never-started runs are distinct. At auth expiry an already-silent relay host is labelled silence timeout without extending authorization. This informs failure classification, without proving our missed runs share the cause.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/40943" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">stablyai/orca · MERGED → main · 2026-11-11T01:43:31Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/40929" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">stablyai/orca · MERGED → main · 2026-11-11T00:19:46Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o20-·-orkas-stop-dispatch-when-compatibility-probes-fail" tabindex="-1">O20 · Orkas: stop dispatch when compatibility probes fail <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-·-orkas-stop-dispatch-when-compatibility-probes-fail" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 · Orkas: stop dispatch when compatibility probes fail&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Failed OpenCode run --help probes stop dispatch instead of selecting commands from empty flags. Failures remain retryable and uncached. Upstream reports a macOS Electron failure/retry journey, without paid-provider, Windows GUI or packaged-build acceptance.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/195" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Orkas-AI/Orkas · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T03:56:18Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o21-·-vibe-kanban-acp-registry-and-dynamic-configuration" tabindex="-1">O21 · Vibe Kanban: ACP registry and dynamic configuration <a class="header-anchor" href="#o21-·-vibe-kanban-acp-registry-and-dynamic-configuration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O21 · Vibe Kanban: ACP registry and dynamic configuration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>ACP registry installs retain chat history, requiring Node/npx and terminal sign-in. A later merge discovers models dynamically and applies model, reasoning then mode; unsupported Plan falls back to Ask, never Auto. New commits justify low-frequency rechecking despite the prior sunset label, not a claim of business revival.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/BloopAI/vibe-kanban/pull/3489" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BloopAI/vibe-kanban · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T06:10:43Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/BloopAI/vibe-kanban/pull/3496" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BloopAI/vibe-kanban · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T10:58:32Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o22-·-openhands-sdk-steering-damaged-events-and-false-success" tabindex="-1">O22 · OpenHands SDK: steering, damaged events and false success <a class="header-anchor" href="#o22-·-openhands-sdk-steering-damaged-events-and-false-success" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O22 · OpenHands SDK: steering, damaged events and false success&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Sockets receive and save steering during running steps, even if clients leave. Corrupt event files become same-ID unreadable placeholders preserving indexes/seq without invented model content. Blocked navigation returns is_error instead of false success.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6709" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OpenHands/software-agent-sdk · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T00:23:30Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6669" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OpenHands/software-agent-sdk · MERGED → main · 2026-11-09T21:20:16Z</a>；<a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6661" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OpenHands/software-agent-sdk · MERGED → main · 2026-11-10T13:08:07Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o23-·-dspy-3-5-runnable-modules-and-migration-cost" tabindex="-1">O23 · DSPy 3.5: runnable modules and migration cost <a class="header-anchor" href="#o23-·-dspy-3-5-runnable-modules-and-migration-cost" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O23 · DSPy 3.5: runnable modules and migration cost&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RLM/Flex/GEPA graduate. ReAct replacement, structured History/typed submit and lm15 routing change prompts, defaults and APIs, requiring re-evaluation of optimized programs. RLM History restores conversations, not live interpreter variables. Stable designation is not a security or durability guarantee.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/releases/tag/3.5.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">stanfordnlp/dspy · RELEASED · 2026-11-10T16:25:47Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o24-·-agentlas-windows-upgrade-boundaries" tabindex="-1">O24 · Agentlas: Windows upgrade boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#o24-·-agentlas-windows-upgrade-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O24 · Agentlas: Windows upgrade boundaries&quot;">​</a></h3><p>An actual older Windows install exposed drive-letter case preventing stale plugin-pin migration. Paths now follow filesystem comparison and avoid sibling-prefix matches; the series also addresses stale binding after host restart. This is scoped upgrade evidence, not universal host coverage.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/agentlas-ai/Agentlas-OS/releases/tag/os-v1.2.95" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">agentlas-ai/Agentlas-OS · RELEASED · 2026-11-09T08:40:54Z</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis. Competitor learning, risk and radar judgments: A6.</p><h3 id="o25-·-langchain-enterprise-platform-case-and-evaluation-method" tabindex="-1">O25 · LangChain: enterprise platform case and evaluation method <a class="header-anchor" href="#o25-·-langchain-enterprise-platform-case-and-evaluation-method" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O25 · LangChain: enterprise platform case and evaluation method&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Nov 10 vendor case study describes Workday combining an internal SDK, LLM/RAG gateways and API governance with LangGraph/LangSmith and server-level A2A/MCP. These are vendor-reported adoption claims, not independent verification. The Nov 9 evaluation guide recommends do/don&#39;t/preserve behavior specifications, state-based outcomes and held-out cases.</p><p><a href="https://www.langchain.com/blog/how-workday-built-an-enterprise-scale-ai-agent-platform-with-langgraph-and-langsmith" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LangChain / Workday · PUBLISHED CASE STUDY · 2026-11-10</a>；<a href="https://www.langchain.com/blog/what-is-eval-driven-development" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LangChain / Workday · PUBLISHED ENGINEERING GUIDE · 2026-11-09</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h3 id="o26-·-openai-business-agents-role-and-authorization-policy" tabindex="-1">O26 · OpenAI: Business Agents role and authorization policy <a class="header-anchor" href="#o26-·-openai-business-agents-role-and-authorization-policy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O26 · OpenAI: Business Agents role and authorization policy&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Nov 10 policy requires honest business/AI representation, accurate information and action within approved role and user authorization, including authorized information collection/transfer. It governs ChatGPT Business Agents representing businesses, not a general multi-agent protocol.</p><p><a href="https://openai.com/policies/business-agents-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OpenAI Business Agents · POLICY UPDATED · 2026-11-10</a></p><p>Verification limit: upstream primary evidence, not locally tested; retain/watch, with candidates in analysis.</p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="a1-·-o3-o4-o5-o6-o15-o18-o26" tabindex="-1">A1 · O3 / O4 / O5 / O6 / O15 / O18 / O26 <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-·-o3-o4-o5-o6-o15-o18-o26" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 · O3 / O4 / O5 / O6 / O15 / O18 / O26&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Authorization follows execution identity and generation; delegated work need not expose secrets. Evidence supports call-time checks, approval ownership and one-time reveal as distinct mechanisms. Test applicability to CodeFlowMu delegation and credential proxies across employees/organizations. This primarily maps to runtime/adapters and product governance, not automatic FCoP-core additions. Candidate probes: identity switch after approval, removed approval owner and concurrent reveal. Discussion: how do approved pending actions expire after authority changes?</p><h3 id="a2-·-o1-o2-o8-o9-o14-o17-o22" tabindex="-1">A2 · O1 / O2 / O8 / O9 / O14 / O17 / O22 <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-·-o1-o2-o8-o9-o14-o17-o22" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 · O1 / O2 / O8 / O9 / O14 / O17 / O22&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Collaborative delivery needs distinct evidence for delivery, acceptance, execution, outcome and recovery. Interrupted records do not prove non-application; transactional receipts strengthen only their protected operations. Test mapping FCoP task/event/artifact semantics to runtime call identities, receipts and unknown outcomes without moving all persistence, scheduling and ownership into the protocol. Candidate probes: lost result after execution, accepted messages without inference, corrupt logs and disconnected steering.</p><h3 id="a3-·-o7-o10-o11-o13-o18-o20-o22" tabindex="-1">A3 · O7 / O10 / O11 / O13 / O18 / O20 / O22 <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-·-o7-o10-o11-o13-o18-o20-o22" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 · O7 / O10 / O11 / O13 / O18 / O20 / O22&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Governance must inspect actual boundaries and failure behavior. Default environment inheritance, advisory conflict tags and readOnly declarations provide different assurances from enforcement. Evidence favors preserving original errors, stopping unsafe dispatch and avoiding false success. Experience candidate: bulbasaur digest/conflict checks, pending installation/license/maintenance review; not installed. Discussion: how is refusal preserved when runtime policy reload fails?</p><h3 id="a4-·-o12-o13-o17-o21-o23-o25" tabindex="-1">A4 · O12 / O13 / O17 / O21 / O23 / O25 <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-·-o12-o13-o17-o21-o23-o25" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 · O12 / O13 / O17 / O21 / O23 / O25&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Compare interoperability by layer: MCP Apps/WebMCP concern view tools, ACP client-agent session configuration, A2A inter-agent interfaces; Orca cross-host coordination still has inert pieces. FCoP file/artifact coordination can complement them; substitution is not established. Experience candidates: ACP-registry apps and AG2/MCP Apps, accounting for Node/login, versions, host support and sandbox cost. DSPy 3.5 needs separate migration evaluation rather than classification as a finished digital employee.</p><h3 id="a5-·-o16-o22-o23-o25" tabindex="-1">A5 · O16 / O22 / O23 / O25 <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-·-o16-o22-o23-o25" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 · O16 / O22 / O23 / O25&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Independent acceptance checks retained state and faults resembling real deployment. Paperclip staging failures and LangChain outcome guidance reinforce a research method, not universal reliability. Candidate experiment: same-host restart versus changed-process-space redeploy, checking task completion, audit and side effects with held-out cases. Discussion: which different-hostHash owner-death ambiguities remain after K15?</p><h3 id="a6-·-o14-o15-o16-o17-o18-o19-o20-o21-o24" tabindex="-1">A6 · O14 / O15 / O16 / O17 / O18 / O19 / O20 / O21 / O24 <a class="header-anchor" href="#a6-·-o14-o15-o16-o17-o18-o19-o20-o21-o24" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A6 · O14 / O15 / O16 / O17 / O18 / O19 / O20 / O21 / O24&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Radar reassessment: Paperclip offers high learning value and high competitive risk in governed operations/recovery, with staging failures limiting reliability confidence. Orca has medium-high multi-device/chat-API risk while cross-host orchestration is incomplete. Orkas and Agentlas offer medium-high compatibility/upgrade learning and medium delivery risk. Keep Vibe Kanban under low-frequency review of the sunset assessment, without inferring business revival. No verified evidence changes commercial-license assessments this round.</p><h2 id="coverage-and-source-type-verification" tabindex="-1">Coverage and source-type verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#coverage-and-source-type-verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Coverage and source-type verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Start: 2026-11-11 10:24:17 Asia/Shanghai. Last successful run: 2026-11-09T022534Z; Nov 10 has no successful execution record. Catch-up uses each source&#39;s last complete baseline without backdated reports. Fresh main Registry has 47 researchers with many-to-many source relationships; Yue Zhao is written 赵越 in Chinese. Initial commits/issues/releases queries cover 88 original repository entries (264 requests). Full 100-item pages are not complete; second pages for three busy commit feeds also remain full, preserving history gaps. TSA-AI-Workforce returns 404, without inferring deletion/privacy. Superset redirects; repository ID 1080370450 verifies ParadevAI/Paradev, whose incremental engineering coverage remains incomplete. Timed-out release calls were retried with ten items; unfinished history stays partial. PR details verify state; merged main is not package delivery except explicit RELEASED entries. All 47 people&#39;s X/replies/threads, author sites, roadmaps/discussions, advisories and license history were not exhausted, nor all README/source files reviewed. Those dimensions do not receive no-change findings or advanced baselines.</p><p>Separate public-web checks: Cursor changelog and Anthropic Engineering (latest displayed Nov 6), plus Yue Zhao&#39;s own homepage; no attributable new in-window item established there. Targeted author/governance searches do not exhaust social activity. LangChain Nov 9–10 publications and OpenAI&#39;s Nov 10 policy supply non-GitHub evidence (O25/O26). GitHub primary evidence can independently support engineering facts; two GitHub links are not two source types.</p><ul><li><a href="https://cursor.com/changelog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cursor</a></li><li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Anthropic Engineering</a></li><li><a href="https://yzhao062.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Yue Zhao</a></li></ul><p>Disposition: 26 observations, six analyses; experience/experiment proposals remain candidates, with no installation or execution of these applications. Completed local research experiments: 0; articles: 0; formal development reviews: 0; external interactions: 0. CodeFlowMu/FCoP links remain unvalidated research leads without development assignment. Public source updates are limited to today&#39;s two reports and two indexes; deployment acceptance is reported in this run&#39;s chat receipt.</p><p>Later manual research update: the zero counts above describe the 10:24 incremental-review snapshot. We subsequently ran an isolated CodeFlowMu task-submission fault injection for A2/O14. With the destination blocked, the call errored and the task stayed in the active folder, while metadata already recorded entry into review. Removing the obstruction allowed the same request to finish with no duplicate transition; retry after a presumed lost success response was rejected by the stage check. Targeted lifecycle tests passed 28/28. This is a bounded local API experiment, neither a Paperclip reproduction nor a production incident. <a href="/joinwell52/en/research/2026-11-11-task-moved-after-record">Bilingual research article</a> · <a href="https://github.com/joinwell52-AI/joinwell52/blob/main/research/manual-runs/2026-11-11-lifecycle-atomicity/00-report.en.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">English evidence</a>. Later manual research completed one experiment question and one bilingual article. CodeFlowMu development value is recorded in a local review; no external interaction was posted merely to meet a count.</p>',126)])])}const m=a(n,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
